; Deep scan follow-up/open-item counter (H-FOLLOWUP-COUNT): change-detector
; test. Unlike the structural smoke tests above, this actually invokes
; check_05_followup_items.sh and check_08_trends.sh against a synthetic
; fixture tree (via the REPO_ROOT env-var override) with a known-correct
; answer — it pins the "- [ ]"-only filter, heading-unscoped counting, and
; the Check 5 -> Check 8 sidecar handoff. Deps list the two underlying
; check scripts + deep_scan/_lib.sh explicitly (not just _check_lib.sh) so
; dune's cache invalidates when their logic changes, not only when this
; test file changes.
;
; H-CHECK-CACHE-BLIND exemption: this script's own repo_root() call
; (REPO_ROOT_REAL) resolves only deep_scan/check_05_followup_items.sh and
; deep_scan/check_08_trends.sh -- both already declared as explicit deps
; above, so their content IS tracked despite the absolute-path read
; escaping the sandbox. The two check scripts are always invoked with
; REPO_ROOT overridden to a synthetic fixture tree, never a real
; outside-workspace file. See universe_deps_exceptions.conf for the
; recorded evidence; no (universe) needed.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  _check_lib.sh
  deep_scan/_lib.sh
  deep_scan/check_05_followup_items.sh
  deep_scan/check_08_trends.sh)
 (action
  (run sh %{dep:deep_scan_followup_count_check.sh})))

; Deep scan rework-streak escalation change-detector test
; (H-REWORK-STREAK-ESCALATION-UNTESTED): actually invokes
; check_06_qc_calibration.sh against a synthetic dev/audit/ fixture (via
; the REPO_ROOT env-var override) with a known-correct answer, same
; pattern as deep_scan_followup_count_check.sh above. Pins the >= 3
; threshold boundary (2 does not fire, 3 and 4 do), the per-feature
; maximum-not-per-record reporting, and the legacy-record (field absent)
; no-crash path for the rework-streak scan that consumes
; write_audit.sh's consecutive_rework_count field. Deps list
; check_06_qc_calibration.sh + deep_scan/_lib.sh explicitly (not just
; _check_lib.sh) so dune's cache invalidates when their logic changes.
;
; Declares (universe): this script's own repo_root() call site
; (REPO_ROOT_REAL) makes it a repo_root()-calling candidate under
; check_universe_deps.sh. Takes the (universe) branch rather than an
; exceptions-list entry: the check under test (check_06's rework-streak
; scan) reads dev/audit/*.json, a real outside-workspace directory whose
; contents change independently of any dune dep list, so a "provably
; already covered or dead" exemption claim would not hold up the way it
; does for deep_scan_followup_count_check.sh's simpler status-file
; fixture. See the open H-UNIVERSE-DEPS-EXEMPTION-EVIDENCE-STALE item for
; why a shaky exemption claim is worth avoiding rather than asserting.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  _check_lib.sh
  deep_scan/_lib.sh
  deep_scan/check_06_qc_calibration.sh
  (universe))
 (action
  (run sh %{dep:deep_scan_rework_streak_check.sh})))

