; Regression test for H-RUNENV-WORKTREE-BLIND: dev/lib/run-in-env.sh's
; in-container path used to pin PROJECT_ROOT to ${GITHUB_WORKSPACE}/trading
; unconditionally, ignoring the invoker's cwd -- an agent running from a git
; worktree would silently build+test the MAIN checkout and report a false
; green. Builds two throwaway git trees in mktemp and asserts the worktree
; case, the normal-GHA case, the devcontainer fallback, and the disagreement
; case (loud failure) all resolve correctly. Does NOT touch the real repo's
; dune-workspace or opam env. Requires bash + git; skips cleanly otherwise.
;
; dev/lib/run-in-env.sh lives outside the dune workspace root (above
; trading/), and the check reads it via repo_root() in _check_lib.sh at
; RUN TIME (a shell function call, not a dune dep) -- a plain (deps ...)
; entry cannot express that path, since dune deps are resolved relative
; to this directory and cannot reach above the workspace root. Without
; (universe), a warm _build treats this rule as fully determined by
; _check_lib.sh + run_in_env_root_check.sh; editing ONLY run-in-env.sh
; leaves the cached PASS result in place and the rule never re-runs,
; silently defeating the regression test it exists to be (confirmed:
; reverting run-in-env.sh to the pre-fix buggy version with a warm
; _build produced exit 0 / zero output -- see PR #2143 review). Any
; check whose script reads a file outside the dune workspace root via
; repo_root() must declare (universe) for the same reason
; (H-CHECK-CACHE-BLIND, dev/status/harness.md).

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps _check_lib.sh run_in_env_root_check.sh (universe))
 (action
  (run sh %{dep:run_in_env_root_check.sh})))

