; Smoke test for posix_sh_check.sh: verifies the linter exits non-zero on a
; known-bad bash-array fixture, exits 0 on a clean POSIX sh script, and exits 0
; on a !/usr/bin/env bash script (exemption check).

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps _check_lib.sh posix_sh_check.sh)
 (action
  (run sh %{dep:posix_sh_check_test.sh})))

; Workflow shellcheck linter (#2521): extracts every `run:` body from
; .github/workflows/*.yml and lints it with shellcheck. Catches variable-
; scoping defects (subshell-modified vars, unbound-under-set-u shapes) that
; `dash -n` (posix_sh_check.sh above) is parse-only and never evaluates, and
; that no other CI gate lints at all. Gracefully SKIPs (exit 0) when
; shellcheck is not on PATH -- not yet in the trading-devcontainer base
; image as of this check's introduction; see workflow_shell_check.sh's own
; header and .devcontainer/Dockerfile.
; Deps: .github/workflows/ is outside the dune workspace root (workspace
; root is trading/) and cannot be tracked via glob_files here, same
; reasoning as posix_sh_check.sh's dev/lib + dev/scripts note above; the
; script reads it via repo_root(), so (universe) forces a re-run whenever
; anything in the repo changes rather than caching a stale PASS.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps _check_lib.sh (universe))
 (action
  (run sh %{dep:workflow_shell_check.sh})))

; Fixture-driven smoke test for workflow_shell_check.sh: builds throwaway
; workflow YAML under a temp dir (never reads real .github/workflows/*.yml),
; and asserts OK on a clean fixture, FAIL naming the file+step on a
; subshell-scope defect (SC2030/SC2031 -- the ce88954 defect class), GH
; ${{ }} expression neutralization, single-line `run:` handling, and the
; shellcheck-absent SKIP path. SKIPs its own shellcheck-dependent assertions
; (still exits 0) when shellcheck is not installed in the running
; environment, so the test itself is green in both worlds.

(rule
