; Smoke test for record_qc_audit.sh: 6 fixture-driven scenarios covering
; file-mode (dev/reviews/<feature>.md), PR-mode (mock gh binary), mixed
; NEEDS_REWORK, non-numeric --pr-number rejection, COMMENTED body-parse,
; and empty-PR-reviews fallback to file mode.
; The test creates its own temp dir fixtures (no real dev/reviews/ or
; dev/audit/ dirs are touched). record_qc_audit.sh, write_audit.sh, and
; _check_lib.sh are declared as deps so the cache key invalidates when any
; of them changes. _check_lib.sh was added for the H-REPO-ROOT-SET-BUT-
; INVALID-SILENT-FALLTHROUGH scenarios (29a-29c): those copy _check_lib.sh
; into a temp fixture and probe its repo_root() directly, so without this
; dep dune's sandbox never copies the file in and the `cp` fails
; (`No such file or directory`) even though the same file is readable
; outside the sandbox.
; Uses `bash` (not `sh`) because the test script uses set -euo pipefail
; and bash-specific constructs (intentional — see #!/usr/bin/env bash shebang).
;
; H-CHECK-CACHE-BLIND exemption: record_qc_audit.sh and write_audit.sh
; each define a private _repo_root() (same walk-up-for-.git/.claude logic
; as _check_lib.sh's repo_root()) and use it to locate dev/reviews/ and
; dev/audit/ -- real outside-workspace paths. But record_qc_audit_test.sh
; invokes both scripts (and, since 29a-29c, _check_lib.sh's repo_root()
; directly) via one of three shapes: (a) REPO_ROOT explicitly overridden
; to a freshly-created temp fixture repo (see the REPO_ROOT="${TMP_REPO}"
; ... invocations throughout the test); (b) REPO_ROOT overridden to a
; deliberately malformed value -- nonexistent path or regular file
; (scenarios 29a/b, 30a/b, 31a/b) -- which the `[ -d ]` guard in
; _repo_root() rejects with a hard error before any path is computed; or
; (c) the walk-up branch, reached either via `env -u REPO_ROOT` or via
; REPO_ROOT='' which _repo_root() treats as unset (scenarios 29c, 30c,
; 31c), from a copy of the script located inside a temp fixture that
; carries its own `.claude` sentinel, e.g. scenarios 27b/28b -- the
; walk-up seeds from the script's own directory (`dirname "$0"`), not the
; caller's CWD, so it terminates inside the fixture regardless of where
; the test runs from. In all three shapes, no real dev/reviews/ or
; dev/audit/ content is ever read by this rule. See
; universe_deps_exceptions.conf.

; record_qc_audit_test.sh's scenario 51 (issue #2591) extracts the
; write_audit.sh FALLBACK code block live from
; .claude/agents/lead-orchestrator.md at the repo root (found via the
; script's own REPO_ROOT walk-up, same as agent_compliance_check.sh below)
; and executes it for real. .claude/agents/*.md is outside the dune
; workspace root, so it can't be declared as a normal glob/file dep (see
; the header note above, line ~18); (universe) is the established pattern
; in this file for exactly that case (agent_compliance_check.sh /
; agent_compliance_test.sh below) -- it also disables dune's per-rule
; sandbox for this rule, so the walk-up can actually reach the real
; .claude/agents/ directory instead of an empty sandboxed one.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps record_qc_audit.sh write_audit.sh _check_lib.sh (universe))
 (action
  (run bash %{dep:record_qc_audit_test.sh})))

; Active exceptions report: lists all linter_exceptions.conf entries and
; inline @large-module / @large-function markers with status (active /
; expired / no-review-at).  Passive — exits 0 always; output goes to the
; build log and can be invoked directly via:
;   dune exec devtools/list_active_exceptions/list_active_exceptions.exe -- <trading-root>
; Cache-invalidated when any .ml file or linter_exceptions.conf changes.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps
  (glob_files_rec %{workspace_root}/*.ml)
  %{workspace_root}/devtools/checks/linter_exceptions.conf)
 (action
  (run
   %{exe:../list_active_exceptions/list_active_exceptions.exe}
   %{workspace_root})))

